<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!-- Delivery dock: the marked drop zone the sample rack is set down on, sitting
     on the ward bench's transfer shelf.

     It exists because the placement is done by visual servo, not dead
     reckoning. Nav2 arrives with roughly 0.2 m of position error, and the
     bench's shelf is only 0.30 m deep against a 0.16 m rack, so a blind place
     from the nav pose has about 0.07 m of margin either side - not enough. The
     mission therefore re-uses the same front-camera colour servo the warehouse
     mission centres on its columns with, and that needs a saturated colour to
     lock onto. A bare steel shelf gives it nothing.

     GREEN, deliberately: the rack's grip block is red, so target and payload
     never share a colour. In the warehouse each column is painted its own box's
     colour, which forces _placement_landed to gate its verification tightly
     enough to keep the pillar out of the blob. Here the post-release check just
     looks for red above the dock and the dock itself cannot be mistaken for it.

     0.08 m tall rather than a flush pad: the front camera sits 0.223 m off the
     floor, so a pad lying flat on a 0.30 m shelf would be viewed almost edge-on
     and segment poorly. This height presents a 0.08 m vertical face at camera z
     +0.077..+0.157, comfortably inside the detection gate.

     Sizing against the shelf it stands on (shelf spans x 13.85..14.15, i.e.
     0.30 deep, and 1.00 m wide): 0.25 x 0.30 leaves the dock fully on the shelf
     with 0.025 m to spare front and back, and gives the 0.16 x 0.12 rack a
     surface with margin all round.

     Model origin is the BOTTOM face, so it spawns at the shelf top height
     (z = 0.30) and its own top - where the rack lands - is at z = 0.38. -->
<sdf version="1.9">
  <model name="delivery_dock">
    <static>true</static>
    <link name="link">
      <collision name="collision">
        <pose>0 0 0.04 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.25 0.30 0.08</size></box></geometry>
        <surface>
          <friction><ode><mu>0.9</mu><mu2>0.9</mu2></ode></friction>
          <contact><ode><kp>1e6</kp><kd>1.0</kd></ode></contact>
        </surface>
      </collision>
      <visual name="visual">
        <pose>0 0 0.04 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.25 0.30 0.08</size></box></geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.05 0.75 0.10 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.06 0.85 0.12 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.15 0.15 0.15 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>
  </model>
</sdf>
